Commit message: 'specification-first' hides that this patch adds 1200 lines of generated
code (`drivers/attestation/generated/*.c`, *.h) that nothing compiles: there is no
`drivers/attestation/Makefile/Kconfig` hook here, and the .c references
`ctlv_attestation_op_pre`/post, `ctlv_attestation_priv_size`, init, `mr_get_action`, ... that
are not defined until later patches. Not building it is what keeps the series
bisectable, but then the generated kernel header/source cannot have been compile-tested at
this point. Please state this explicitly. I regenerated the tree at this commit
(`tools/ctlv/ctlv-regen.sh` -c, validate, abi-check): all pass, so the generated files do
match the spec.

