The device.generation attribute (ID 1, max 4294967295) appears in no attr-set and no op:
device-reply carries only device.caps and device.info. It is dead UAPI, yet it burns attr
ID 1 of group 'device', adds the exported `CTLV_ATTESTATION_ATTR_DEVICE_GENERATION` macro and
an unused `ctlv_attestation_device_generation_put()` inline in the kernel header. Remove it;
an attribute can be added compatibly when the feature arrives. The ABI snapshot treats
removal as a break, so adding it now makes it permanent.

