The three capability lengths (min-challenge-length, max-challenge-length,
max-total-output-length) and cap.max-length / evidence.object-length are 'type: uint'
without a max, i.e. generated with `U64_MAX` bounds, whereas their consumers are bounded:
evidence.challenge has max-length 4096, evidence.data has max-length 4294967295 (`U32_MAX`).
A provider could therefore advertise a max-challenge-length of 2^63 that the request
schema can never accept. Bound them to the same limits in the spec (and the ABI would then
need no later narrowing, which is by its own rule a break).

