member list (name, supported-hash-algo, caps, optional register-index; mr-dump-entry adds
id), mr-id-request and mr-read-request are identical (just mr.id) and mr-log-selection
is a third copy of {mr.id}. Each set takes an ID and is part of the ABI registry (sets
1..23 are frozen in the snapshot), and each costs a node-schema array in the generated
code. Define one set and reuse it (op-specific naming buys nothing, stubs are the only
place where a set ID is externally visible).

