The put/nest helpers are emitted for every attribute of every group, regardless of
whether any reply uses it (e.g. `ctlv_attestation_evidence_challenge_put`,
`ctlv_attestation_evidence_blob_class_put`, `ctlv_attestation_mr_selection_start` and
...`_mr_start_generation_put` are request-only attributes and are never written by the
kernel; conversely `ctlv_attestation_device_generation_put` is unused entirely). All are
static inline so there are no unused warnings, but it makes the writable surface of
replies untyped relative to the schema (the validation then happens at runtime).

