Summary:
 - I regenerated at this commit (`ctlv-regen.sh` -c, validate, abi-check): generated files match
   the spec and ABI snapshot, so no generator mismatch found.
 - UAPI/ABI quality: device.generation is dead (unused by any set or op) yet frozen in the
   ABI; hash-algo 'max: 20' / 21 occurrences are unexplained magic numbers against
   `hash_info.h` (which now extends to 22); capability lengths are unbounded (`U64_MAX`) while
   consumers are bounded; evidence-get requires read-write fd access with no rationale.
 - Spec redundancy: mr-props / mr-dump-entry / mr-log-info, mr-id-request / mr-read-request /
   mr-log-selection are near-identical sets, each burning a permanent set ID; 'mr-log-event'
   names an enum and a set and the event's reply set.
 - Series/commit message: 1200 lines of generated C/H that are not built and reference ~13
   undefined functions; commit message should say so. Single-valued enums are speculative.
 - MAINTAINERS uses a different e-mail than patch 13; accessor names are stuttered and do not
   match the naming documented in patch 13.
